🎯 Program 12 — Random Access in a Binary File

📌 Description

This program demonstrates how to directly access a selected record in a binary file without reading every previous record.

The program calculates the byte offset of a fixed-size record and uses "seekg()" to move directly to that position.

🔑 Concepts Covered

- 🎯 Random access
- 💾 Binary files
- 📦 Fixed-size records
- 📍 File offsets
- "seekg()"
- "read()"

📁 File Created

"records.dat"

🧠 Main Concept

Directly locate and read a selected binary record
